{"name":"Swan Dive","hex":"#e5e4dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swan dive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A forward dive performed with an arched back, the legs together, starting with arms outstretched when jumping, bringing them over the head when landing.","A similar movement out of the water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swan_dive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swan Dive","blocks":[{"text":"Swan Dive is an American musical duo composed of Bill DeMain and Molly Felder. Founded in 1995, Swan Dive is best known for its album Circle, released in 1998."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swan_Dive","wikidata":"Q7653437"},{"title":"Swan","blocks":[{"text":"Swans are birds of the genus Cygnus within the family Anatidae. The swans' closest relatives include geese and ducks. Swans are grouped with the closely related geese in the subfamily Anserinae, forming the tribe Cygnini. Sometimes, they are considered a distinct subfamily, Cygninae. They are the largest waterfowl and are often among the largest flighted birds in their range."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mute_Swan_Emsworth2.JPG/330px-Mute_Swan_Emsworth2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swan","wikidata":"Q29564928"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg/500px-Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg/1280px-Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg/500px-Mute_swan_family_with_five_cygnets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam